  "title": "Homemade Olive Tapenade",
  "description": "The anchovies are very salty. If you find your tapenade too salty, add more olives or olive oil.",
  "editorial": {
    "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The homemade olive tapenade is a dip or paste made with olives (black or green), anchovies and capers. This appetizer comes from Provence, France and is great with fresh bread or toast. With the help of a food processor, or blender, this hors d'oeuvre is ready within 5 minutes.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe {\"id\":21335,\"template\":\"chic-template-english\",\"updated\":1608951341260} -->\n<!--WPRM Recipe 21335-->\n<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe\">\n\t<h2 class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-name\">Homemade Olive Tapenade</h2>\n\t<img class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-image\" src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/07/IMG_1600.Blog_-150x150.png\"/>\t<p class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-summary\">\n\t\tThe anchovies are very salty. If you find your tapenade too salty, add more olives or olive oil. \r\n\t</p>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-equipment\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-ingredients\">\n\t\t<ul><li>200 g black olives (pitted)</li><li>1 Tbsp capers ((optional))</li><li>20 g anchovies filets in oil</li><li>2 cloves garlic</li><li>1/2 lemon (juice only)</li><li>4  Tbsp olive oil</li><li>freshly ground black pepper (to taste)</li></ul>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-instructions\">\n\t\t<ol><li>Combine all ingredients in an electric blender. Pulse a few times until finely chopped. The tapenade should have small pieces of olives. Do not over blend!<br /><img src=\"https://mycafegourmand.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/07/IMG_1583.Blog_-150x150.png\"/><br /></li><li>Serve with crackers or fresh baguette slices. </li></ol>\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-notes\">\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta\">\n\t\t<div class=\"wprm-fallback-recipe-meta-course\">Appetizers</div>\t</div>\n</div>\n<!--End WPRM Recipe-->\n<!-- /wp:wp-recipe-maker/recipe -->",
    "excerpt": null
  },
